{
  "dom_id": "step-q136890",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "A discrete random variable $X$ has the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below.  Find $\\text{E}[\\sqrt[3]{X}].$\n\n| $x$ | $8$ | $27$ | $64$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ |",
  "worked_solution": "For a discrete random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}r(x)f(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nr(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\sqrt[3]{X}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}\\sqrt[3]{x}\\,f(x) \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{8}\\cdot 0.4+\\sqrt[3]{27}\\cdot 0.4+\\sqrt[3]{64}\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.4+3\\cdot 0.4+4\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0.8+1.2+0.8 \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
